<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second World War</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as World War II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second World War was the global conflict of 1939 to 1945 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis powers</a>, the deadliest war in history. It destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a>, whose African colonies were lost to Allied forces, and fatally weakened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>, accelerating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/decolonisation">decolonisation</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a> also refer to it in discussing the troubled fate of the successor states of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-world-war.jpg" alt="Second World War" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Richard Opitz · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_101I-646-5188-17,_Flugzeuge_Junkers_Ju_87.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
